{"t": 69.832, "n": 89, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I built all four rows of Phase 6 (6.1 to 6.4) and marked them completed with 2026-11-26. `test_regeneration_records.py` passed: 5 tests. I did not run any other test file.\n\n- **6.1:** I wrote the new test file first. Three of its five tests failed for the right reasons (revision still 24, README had no `regeneration` row, one test name written in lower case). I then widened the criterion-id check to accept ids written in lower case, such as `rgn_ac4`.\n- **6.2:** `outcome.json` is at revision 25. It has an `intermediate.regeneration` entry with three criteria, `ts-rgn-declaration`, `ts-rgn-ran` and `ts-rgn-passed`. Each is a `check` criterion that serves `ts-accepted` and runs `regeneration_check`. Revision record 25 is appended, and I wrote no digest.\n- **6.3:** The README has a `regeneration` row between `code` and `independent_review`. All three lane rows show the unit after `code`.\n- **6.4:** CON-B7 now lists `on_fail` as `retry`, `stop`, `fallback` or `back` with a link to HUM-B15.\n\nShell `sed` was denied, so I marked the plan rows with the Edit tool instead. I made no deviations from the plan.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran plugins/temperspec-tgraph/tests/test_regeneration_records.py (5 passed, first run had 3 expected failures before the docs rows). Built rows 6.1-6.4 and marked them in the plan. Deviations: none. The code report must still name the stamp.json, authoring.json and diagram/ files of the package as left for the operator.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "e3406db8-559d-46d2-9da7-42e8d6841247"}
